.TH cksum 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
cksum \- print a CRC checksum and byte count
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cksum
[\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cksum
prints a checksum, a byte count and the name for each
.IR file .
With no
.IR file ,
or with
.BR \- ,
it reads standard input and prints no name.
.PP
The checksum is the 32-bit CRC of ISO/IEC 8802-3, which is what POSIX
specifies, so the numbers agree with
.B cksum
on other systems.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH NOTES
This is a different and much stronger checksum than
.BR sum (1),
and the two never agree.
.SH EXIT STATUS
1 if any file could not be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sum (1),
.BR cmp (1),
.BR wc (1)
